.TH diskviz "1" "" "The scalpel3 Disk Visualizer" "The scalpel3 Disk Visualizer"

.SH NAME
diskviz \- Visualize synthetic disk image layouts

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diskviz
\fIkeyfile\fR
[\fB-d\fR \fIbasedir\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBdiskviz\fR reads a \fI.key\fR file produced by \fBfragmentator\fR(1) and renders an interactive GUI visualization of the disk image layout using SDL2.
.PP
The visualization displays each disk block as a cell in a grid. Image files (PNG, JPG, GIF) are rendered as tiled image blocks showing the actual image content. Non-visual file types (ZIP, ELF, RAR, MP3, PDF, etc.) are shown as distinctly colored labeled blocks. RANDOM fill blocks are rendered as colorful noise and ZERO fill blocks display repeating "0" characters.
.PP
The tool opens in the "originals" view, showing all files unfragmented side by side. Pressing SPACEBAR toggles to the "jigsaw" view, which shows the fragmented disk layout as it actually appears on the synthetic disk image.

.SH OPTIONS
.PP
.TP
.BI -d " basedir"
Base directory for resolving file paths referenced in the key file. If not specified, paths are resolved relative to the current working directory.

.SH INTERACTION
.PP
.TP
.B SPACEBAR
Toggle between the original files view and the jigsaw (fragmented) view.
.TP
.B LEFT ARROW
Switch to the original files view.
.TP
.B RIGHT ARROW
Switch to the jigsaw (fragmented) view.
.TP
.B Q / ESC
Quit the application. Works from both the terminal and the graphical window. SPACEBAR and arrow keys also work from either.
.TP
.B Mouse hover
In jigsaw view, hover over a block to see a tooltip with the file name, block number, and block type.
.TP
.B Window resize
The grid automatically recomputes to fill the window.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fragmentator (1),
.BR scalpel3 (1)

